                <head>No. 138.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Denby to Mr. Bayard</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1886-12-18"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 18, 1886</date>.
                        (Received February 12, 1887.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 273.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform the Department
                    of the appointment of Marquis Tseng, late Chinese minister to England and
                    Russia, as minister of the Tsung-li yamên. I will only say that his appointment
                    is regarded as a good one.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Denby.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
